{"changes":["plugin/registry.go: New: hardcoded official registry `OfficialRegistry` (type Registry with unexported entries map) mapping plugin name -\u003e Repo{Owner,Name} (today: \"mcp\" -\u003e maleolabs/eka-mcp). Minimal API per the trust-model follow-up: Lookup(name) (Repo, bool), IsOfficial(name) bool, Names() []string (sorted, for the unknown-name refusal). Official entries are full-trust by definition of the two-tier trust model; today the registry only resolves the source repository.","plugin/plugin.go: Extended Manifest additively per the cross-repo contract pin (contract stays v1): `Capabilities []string` (json:\"capabilities\") and `Source string` (json:\"source\"), both optional/absent for legacy manifests; standard encoding/json ignores unknown fields, so newer manifests parse fine. Added exported `PluginDir(home)` accessor (the install target: $EKA_PLUGIN_DIR or \u003chome\u003e/.eka/plugins, first entry of DefaultPluginPaths) — DefaultPluginPaths semantics unchanged.","cmd/plugin.go: New: `eka plugin` command group + `eka plugin install \u003cname\u003e`. Installer lives in a `pluginInstallRunner` (injectable resolve func, apiBase/downloadRoot, http.Client, pluginDir, goos/goarch, version) mirroring the update command's testable design: package-level endpoint vars + phase-timed client, per-request deadlines (no global Client.Timeout). Reuses update.go's checksumForAsset / sha256File / barWriter / latestDownloadMarker helpers. Fail-closed at every step; refusals exit 1, usage errors exit 2. User-Agent \"eka-cli/\u003cversion\u003e\" on the GitHub API; 403/429 with X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0 yields a clear rate-limit error.","cmd/update.go: Refactor: extracted `platformAssetName(prefix, goos, goarch)` from `updateAssetName` (behavior identical; existing update tests untouched) so plugin install shares the exact platform validation and the eka-\u003cos\u003e-\u003carch\u003e[.exe] naming contract.","cmd/root.go: Registered `newPluginCommand()` in the command tree; doc comments updated (command tree list, allowed-imports list now includes plugin/, root Long text).","cmd/execute_test.go: Expected update: the unknown-command message lists the registered commands alphabetically; added \"plugin\" (between note and project).","plugin/plugin_test.go: fakeExe now emits the eka-mcp manifest shape (capabilities [install mcp], source github.com/maleolabs/eka-mcp). New tests: TestManifestLegacyWithoutCapabilities (optional fields, empty when absent) and TestManifestUnknownFieldsIgnored (forward-compatible parsing).","plugin/registry_test.go: New: pins the registry entries and the lookup API (Lookup/IsOfficial/Names, unknown names refused).","cmd/plugin_test.go: New: hermetic httptest suite. fakePluginReleaseServer serves release metadata (asserts the eka-cli User-Agent + GitHub Accept header), tag-pinned SHA256SUMS.txt and the binary asset; the downloaded 'binary' is a shell script implementing the contract so the manifest smoke check runs without a real plugin. Covers: happy path (install + discoverability = acceptance criterion 1), unknown name, checksum mismatch / missing entry / malformed entry (fail-closed = acceptance criterion 2), broken manifest, manifest name mismatch, rate limit, reinstall overwrite + notice, unsupported platform, asset naming table, command tree/help."],"role":"implementation","summary":"Implemented the hardcoded official plugin registry (plugin/registry.go: name -\u003e GitHub repo) and the `eka plugin install \u003cname\u003e` command. The install flow resolves the plugin name through the registry, determines the latest release via the GitHub REST API (minimal eka-cli User-Agent, clear rate-limit error), downloads the platform asset `eka-\u003cname\u003e-\u003cos\u003e-\u003carch\u003e[.exe]` and SHA256SUMS.txt from the SAME tag-pinned release, verifies the SHA-256 fail-closed (any mismatch/missing/malformed entry refuses and deletes the partial download), installs the verified binary as `eka-\u003cname\u003e` (0755) into the plugin dir ($EKA_PLUGIN_DIR or ~/.eka/plugins) and smoke-checks it by running `manifest` (must parse into plugin.Manifest with a matching name; a broken manifest removes the binary and refuses). Re-install overwrites cleanly with a printed notice. Extended the plugin.Manifest contract additively (v1 stays v1, backward-compatible): Capabilities ([]string) + Source (string) per the cross-repo contract pin with eka/sto:mcp-manifest-capabilities (eka-mcp emits exactly capabilities:[\"install\",\"mcp\"], source:\"github.com/maleolabs/eka-mcp\"). No new dependencies (stdlib net/http only); all network is injectable (httptest in tests).","tests":["go build ./... — clean","go vet ./... — clean","gofmt -l . — clean (no unformatted files)","GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./cmd/eka — windows cross-compile gate passes","go test ./... — 578 passed, 0 failed","go test -race -count=1 ./... — 578 passed, 0 failed (CI unit-test gate)"]}